                        <forename>Thomas</forename>
                        <surname>Cadell</surname>
                        <addName>Thomas Cadell the elder</addName>
                    </persName>
                    <birth when="1742-11-12">
                        <placeName> </placeName>
                    </birth>
                    <death when="1802-12-27"/>
                    <occupation>bookseller</occupation>
                    <note type="editorial">
                        <p>Cadell was an eminent London publisher whose <persName key="CAD01">son</persName>  took over his  business in 1793. 
  Godwin notes that there is a dinner to celebrate Gibbon's birthday and day of publication on 8 May 1788 held at Caddel's, although it is not entirely clear whether Godwin is reporting it, or whether he attended it.
  Notable publications included Gibbon's <title>Decline and Fall of the Roman Empire</title> (1776-88), Mackenzie's <title>The Man of Feeling</title> (1771), and 
    the poetry of Robert Burns.</p>
                    </note>
                    <bibl type="other"><title>The British Book Trade Index</title>, www.bbti.bham.ac.uk.</bibl>
